rows.en:
Kidding, kidding, I'm only joking.
Anyway, the thing is, weird stuff comes out of the taps at this school too.
Stuff that normally never comes out of a tap.{p}

So Shida stayed friends with her, but then apparently her show-business debut got officially settled.
So she didn't need Tamai or the money anymore.
And that's when she turned cold.{p}

You know, the drinking fountain next to the gym.
The one where the guys from the sports clubs gulp down water after practice and stuff.
Just the second faucet from the right can't be used, right?{p}

When they reached the fountains, Miyagi gulped the water down like it was delicious.
"Thank you.
I'm fine now."{p}

But eventually, strange rumors started going around about those fountains.
That at two in the morning the second faucet from the right would be left running, that a girl's ghost appeared in the evening, all kinds of things.
After an incident like that, everyone was whispering that it was Miyagi's ghost coming out.{p}

And the way she did it was flashy, or bold, or something...
She burned herself to death.
She snuck out of the house at night, and on the embankment of that reservoir near this school, she doused herself in kerosene and set herself on fire.{p}

The strange thing is, after the fire went out, there was nothing left at all.
Not her body, not even her bones.
Everyone who was there saw her, so I think she really did burn up completely.{p}

Well, from that day on, it changed to a black, slimy liquid like oil coming out.
This rumor was true: no matter how much they checked the pipes, the faucet and the water tank, they couldn't find anything wrong.
The other faucets were perfectly fine, but only that one gave out a weird liquid.{p}

Right, {b}, you're pretty famous, after all.
You probably can't understand people who get all happy or upset over little things like this.
Ha ha, I'm not blaming you or anything.{p}

One day, after P.E., as Sugiura was heading back to the classroom, she heard a voice from somewhere.
A faint, thin voice that sounded like it was calling for help.
She immediately went looking for whoever it was.{p}

The voice seemed to come from the back of the gym, from the gym storeroom.
"I didn't hear anything when I put the balls away just now..."
Muttering that, she went toward the voice.{p}

That's right.
She tried to go get them some water.
The closest place from there was the drinking fountains beside the gym.{p}

Maybe because they were so thin, both children were very light.
So she reached the fountains in no time.
And then...☆{p}

A searing pain shot through the side of her neck!
The little sister had sunk her teeth into Sugiura's neck!
Then an agonizing pain in her right hand too...!{p}

And then they vanished, as if they'd been sucked into the faucet.
The water that had been gushing out got sucked back into the faucet too, like a film running backward.
She just stood there stunned for a while, it seems.{p}

You know the drinking fountain beside the gym, right?
The one where the guys from the sports clubs gulp down water after practice and stuff.
Haven't you ever noticed that only the second faucet from the right there can't be used?{p}

Like that the two of them were hugging alone in the classroom after school, or that Shida was crying and giving Tamai a hard time... there were too many to count...
I don't know if those rumors were true or not.
After all, rumors are just rumors...{p}

Maybe everyone was jealous of the two of them being so close.
And, sorry to you since you answered "angel," but she was human after all.
One day, out of nowhere, the two of them fell out.{p}

Hmm.
So you think so too?
No matter how good a person is, in the end they're only human.{p}

And if you touch that liquid by accident, your skin looks like the color's been drained out of it, and it doesn't go back to normal for a while.
So, since the students found it creepy, the teachers sealed the faucet.
Does the fishy liquid still come out now, you ask?{p}
